    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21i51nf5mHWex3PPP3SRwVN)_\n\n## Summary\n`M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex` made Emacs unresponsive. It was not a missing file: every author note was compared with every author of every entry (people × entries × authors, each comparison allocating strings). With #229's slices it still froze, because one author note is one indivisible step and took seconds on a big `.bib`.\n\n- The entries without a litnote are indexed once (new \"indexing\" stage) by full author name and by last name plus first initial; a note looks up only its own keys. Results and their order are unchanged.\n- Missing files: a file of `sp-bibtex-files` that cannot be read is skipped with a message. No files, or none readable, stops with a `user-error` naming them and suggesting `sp-bibtex-register`.\n- Doc (`sp-org-lint.org`) tangled, CHANGELOG entry added.\n\n## Measurements (synthetic vault, Emacs 29.3)\n- 3,000 author notes, 500 entries: 48.7 s before.\n- 3,000 author notes, 40,000 entries (31 MB `.bib`), 5,000 litnotes: about 7 s after (3.8 s reading the `.bib`), in slices. Before, extrapolated, hours.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] ERT `tests/sp-author-notes-bibtex-test.el`: 7 pass (new: no files, missing file skipped, 3,000 entries × 1,500 people).\n- [x] `tools/tangle-all.el`; only the doc's own `.el` differs.\n- [ ] Try `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex` on the real vault with `master.bib`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9HDQBXXdZ9XpEdeVx)_",
